                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#c" cert="low"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_437">Winchester, Hampshire.
                        Benedictine cathedral priory of St Peter, St Paul, and St Swithun</orgName><p>Saints culted at both Old and New Minsters are in the text, but
                        the provision of an 'Oratio in noui monasterii ecclesia' would suggest the
                        New Minster. The immediately preceding entry, with prayer addressed to the
                        Virgin and all her virgins, probably relates to the new tower of the New
                        Minster that was erected in the 980s, probably at the north-west end of the
                        building, and which included at ground level a porticus dedicated to the
                        Virgin. The processional route that is here outlined seems to be from the
                        Old Minster to the church of St Gregory (at the south-west corner of New
                        Minster), the procession then moving from the porticus chapel of St Mary
                        into the main body of the New Minster.</p><p>(This pers. comm. from Derek
                        Keene, 2016; discussion to appear in the Historic Town Atlas volume on
                        Winchester, and text and discussion to appear in Winchester Studies vol.
                        4/1.)</p><p> Normal 0 false false false MicrosoftInternetExplorer4 </p><q type="pressmark"> Normal 0 false false false MicrosoftInternetExplorer4
                     </q></provenance>
